{
  "_about": "What each boundary set is and where it comes from: DataSF dataset, join key, name field, fields kept, matching rules. Copied from civic-joy-fund/joiner config/layers.json (2026-10-27, v42); aliases moved to data/aliases.json. 'tab' and the label fields are Joiner's display settings and will move back to Joiner.",
  "_doc": "Boundary layers Joiner can join to. scripts/get_layers.py downloads each from DataSF and writes data/boundaries/<id>.geojson plus data/boundaries/index.json. key = feature property rows are joined on; name = label shown in the side panel; keep = properties kept (all others dropped). Neighborhood sets appear in the Neighborhood tab in the order listed here; \"default\": true marks the one it opens with. match = how row values are normalized before matching: stripPrefix (regex, case-insensitive), caseInsensitive, collapseSpace, delimiter (split one cell into several keys, e.g. a multi-select \"1,3\"). nameTemplate (optional) builds the label from properties, e.g. \"District {sup_dist}\". labelTemplate (optional) is the short ID drawn on the map, e.g. \"D{sup_dist}\". labelExtras are extra label lines the map can show for that layer: prop to read, lastWord to keep only the last word, template with {} for the value, default to show it without being picked. localFiles (instead of dataset) builds a layer from GeoJSON already in the repo. In labelExtras, hover shows the line in the hover tooltip and popup, list shows it in the area list, values maps raw values to text. short (optional) is the name shown on a tab when the full label is long. tab \"Other\" puts a layer in the Other menu (the tabs are made from the tab names, in config order; Other is always last, with Upload). regional marks a layer beyond SF: the map zooms to all of it. dissolve {from, by} builds a layer by merging another layer's features that share a property (precincts into districts); the source must be listed first.",
  "portal": "https://data.sf.gov",
  "precision": 6,
  "mainlandBbox": [
    -122.53,
    37.7,
    -122.34,
    37.84
  ],
